## Usage

- This spec is the authoritative-rule entry point and keeps only current constraints and synchronization coverage. Source-learned content is routed by responsibility to the project overview, business patterns, and capability entry index.
{{if .References.ProjectOverview}}- For the architecture map read [Project Overview](./project-overview.md){{if .References.KeyModules}}; for module details read [Key Modules](./modules.md){{end}}{{if .References.BusinessMethods}}; for capability entries read [Capability Entry Index](./business-methods.md){{end}}.{{end}}
- Category patterns describe behavioral patterns and reuse boundaries; {{if .References.BusinessMethods}}the [Capability Entry Index](./business-methods.md){{else}}the capability entry index{{end}} locates verified capabilities, while individual details contain signatures, prerequisites, return semantics, and usage scenarios.
- Authoritative rules only come from user-maintained or built-in constraints. Source-learned results are reuse and safety inspection entries only.
- Explicit authoritative rules outrank current code and learned references. Current code may only correct a stale source-learned summary; it cannot override or relax authoritative constraints.

